  "comment:typescript": "Pinned to 5.9 LTS, NOT the 7.0.2 in CLAUDE.md's stack table. typescript-eslint 8.67.0 hard-throws on TS >= 7.0 and support only returns with TS 7.1 (typescript-eslint#10940), which takes the whole ESLint gate down — and that gate is the TEN-02/TEN-05 enforcement mechanism, so it cannot be sacrificed. CLAUDE.md pre-authorizes exactly this: 'if any tool in your chain (ESLint plugin, codegen) throws obscure errors, pin to TypeScript 5.9 LTS as a fallback'. Revert to 7.0.2 in one line once typescript-eslint ships TS >= 7.1 support.",
